removed after visual inspection."},"assets_remove":["figure","figure_caption"],"reasons":["Answer independently checked against the complete statement and all options; required visuals inspected.","Remove unrelated cover artwork; preserve the answer and all attempt records.","The complete linear model is given in text."]},{"id":"ed76ef45-9030-5378-b804-4c4650a634ea","row_hash":"38994589ae41c2796204f3b249acabee","key_hash":"bd6032dd175141b86eb3f273dfe3a163","fields":{"explanation":"The original mean is (91 + 96 + 88 + 91 + 84)/5 = 90. Adding 100 makes the mean 550/6 ≈ 91.67, an increase. The sorted data become 84, 88, 91, 91, 96, 100; both the old median and new median are 91. Thus C is correct."},"assets_merge":{"bank_review_release":"20261114-bank-review","bank_review_date":"2026-11-14","verified_release":"20261114-bank-review","answer_review_status":"independently_solved"},"assets_remove":[],"reasons":["Answer independently checked against the complete statement and all options; required visuals inspected.","Replace answer-sheet reference with an independently worked explanation."]},{"id":"f071a174-ffa8-5c12-b7d7-45d4c9dec57f","row_hash":"66ea8c9c14df8f008d0b928a52e8f50e","key_hash":"7ae6c88d62d56157b21ded4670be1c34","fields":{"explanation":"A sample mean of 7 minutes with margin of error 2 minutes gives the plausible interval 7 ± 2, or 5 to 9 minutes, for the population mean. It does not describe every individual wait or rule out all population means outside the interval. Therefore C is the appropriate conclusion."},"assets_merge":{"bank_review_release":"20261114-bank-review","bank_review_date":"2026-11-14","verified_release":"20261114-bank-review","answer_review_status":"independently_solved"},"assets_remove":[],"reasons":["Answer independently checked against the complete statement and all options; required visuals inspected.","Replace answer-sheet reference with an independently worked explanation."]},{"id":"f5d0090b-a4f8-52f2-9a11-f494df25aee0","row_hash":"e3