20261114-bank-review","bank_review_date":"2026-11-14","figure_required":true,"display_repair":"Unrelated cover image removed after visual inspection.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 520 300\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Parallel lines AB and CD, crossing segments AD and BC, and labeled exterior angles\"><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"white\"/><path d=\"M80.000 55.000L460.000 55.000\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#173a55\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><path d=\"M80.000 245.000L460.000 245.000\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#173a55\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><path d=\"M255.701 55.000L344.299 245.000\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#173a55\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><path d=\"M249.488 245.000L350.512 55.000\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#173a55\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"255.701\" y=\"43.000\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#173a55\">A</text><text x=\"350.512\" y=\"43.000\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#173a55\">B</text><text x=\"249.488\" y=\"270.000\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#173a55\">C</text><text x=\"344.299\" y=\"270.000\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#173a55\">D</text><text x=\"276.000\" y=\"155.000\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#173a55\">E</text><text x=\"82.000\" y=\"43.000\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#173a55\">U</text><text x=\"82.000\" y=\"272.000\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#173a55\">V</text><text x=\"185.701\" y=\"91.000\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#173a55\">115°</text><text x=\"184.488\" y=\"218.000\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#173a55\">118°</text><text x=\"317.000\" y=\"156.000\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#173a55\">x°</text><text x=\"385.000\" y=\"159.000\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#173a55\">AB ∥ CD</text></svg>","content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor diagram defines the two exterior angles and the requested angle; it is not claimed to be a recovered source image.","source_original_stem":"In the diagram AB∥CD, AD and BC cross at E. If y=115° and z=118°, find x."},"assets_remove":["figure","figure_caption"],"reasons":["Remove unrelated cover artwork; preserve the answer and all attempt records.","Explicit instructor diagram defines the two exterior angles and the requested angle; it is not claimed to be a recovered source image."]},{"id":"38b3ea7c-1a64-5d12-8944-dedd2448b7c9","row_hash":"8ada3f2ddc938a1a197833ffe1ccee27","key_hash":"447dd71a817193c813929276e4cc7e4d","fields":{"stem":"In right triangle RST, angle T is 90° and tan R = 140/171. An acute angle X in a similar right triangle is equal to angle S. What is sin X?","explanation":"Take ST = 140 and RT = 171. The hypotenuse is √(140² + 171²) = 221. Since X = S, sin X = RT/RS = 171/221, choice C."},"assets_merge":{"bank_review_release":"20261114-bank-review","bank_review_date":"2026-11-14","figure_required":false,"display_repair":"Unrelated cover image removed after visual inspection.","content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor clarification supplies the right angle and angle correspondence missing from the unrelated image.","source_original_stem":"Triangles RST and XYZ are similar, with XY parallel to TS. Given tan R=140/171, find sin X."},"assets_remove":["figure","figure_caption"],"reasons":["Remove unrelated cover artwork; preserve the answer and all attempt records.","Explicit instructor clarification supplies the right angle and angle correspondence missing from the unrelated image."]},{"id":"5b49ca69-bdf0-5859-b0c5-c8d1b68ccb9f","row_hash":"bcbdaddc3fd6a132ac8d15e629123dda","key_hash":"8f80b7428ffa30e2f087944fd62bfe50","fields":{},"assets_merge":{"bank_review_release":"20261114-bank-review","bank_review_date":"2026-11-14","figure_required":false,"display_repair":"Unrelated cover image removed after visual inspection."},"assets_remove":["figure","figure_caption"],"reasons":["Remove unrelated cover artwork; preserve the answer and all attempt records."]},{"id":"b18f2a3d-941e-5ee7-92f4-f883d6c69473","row_hash":"483056ee2cdee9fae52a48d109fb3091","key_hash":"e433163e311c3a7f9ac983b4e5